## Overview

These scripts download video files from AWS S3 buckets organized in a time-based directory structure:
```
s3://bucket/location/YYYY/MM/DD/HH/filename.mp4
```

**Two Scripts:**
- **`downloader.sh`** - One-time historical downloads
- **`continuous_downloader.sh`** - Real-time continuous downloads

---

# One-Time Downloader

## Purpose

Downloads files from S3 for a specific time range and exits. Perfect for:
- Backfilling historical data
- Downloading specific time periods
- One-off data retrieval

## Features

✅ **Flexible Time Ranges**
- Start to end time
- Start to current time
- Beginning to end time

✅ **Smart Processing**
- Lists hour-by-hour directories
- Sorts files chronologically before downloading
- Parallel listing and downloading (streams via FIFO)

✅ **Performance**
- Configurable parallel downloads (default: 10)
- No duplicate checking (downloads everything)
- No state tracking (stateless execution)

✅ **Filtering**
- Filter by channel numbers
- Time-range precision (minute-level)

