## Usage

### Basic Examples

```bash
# 1. Download specific time range
./downloader.sh --start "2025-11-07 10:25" --end "2025-11-07 11:30"

# 2. Download from start to now
./downloader.sh --start "2025-11-07 10:25"

# 3. Download everything up to end time
./downloader.sh --end "2025-11-07 11:30"

# 4. Download specific channels only
./downloader.sh \
  --start "2025-11-07 10:00" \
  --end "2025-11-07 12:00" \
  --channel "401,701"

# 5. Single channel
./downloader.sh --start "2025-11-07 10:00" --channel "401"
```

### Time Format

```
YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM
│    │  │  │  │
│    │  │  │  └─ Minutes (00-59)
│    │  │  └──── Hours (00-23, IST timezone)
│    │  └─────── Day (01-31)
│    └────────── Month (01-12)
└─────────────── Year (4 digits)

Examples:
  2025-11-07 10:25  ✓
  2025-11-07 09:00  ✓
  2025-1-7 9:0      ✗ (must be zero-padded)
```

### Channel Format

```bash
# Single channel
--channel "401"

# Multiple channels (comma-separated)
--channel "401,701,301"

# With brackets (optional)
--channel "[401,701]"

# All channels (omit flag)
./downloader.sh --start "..." --end "..."
```

