## Performance Tips

### 1. Adjust Parallelism

```bash
# Edit script
MAX_PARALLEL=20  # More workers for faster downloads

# Trade-offs:
# More workers = Faster but more CPU/network
# Fewer workers = Slower but more stable
```

### 2. Network Optimization

```bash
# Use EC2 instance in same region as S3
# Enable S3 Transfer Acceleration (if available)
aws configure set default.s3.max_concurrent_requests 20
```

### 3. Large Time Ranges

```bash
# Break into smaller chunks
./downloader.sh --start "2025-11-01 00:00" --end "2025-11-01 23:59"
./downloader.sh --start "2025-11-02 00:00" --end "2025-11-02 23:59"
# ... etc
```

---

## Limitations

❌ **No duplicate detection** - Downloads everything (no check for existing files)
❌ **No resume** - Starts fresh each time
❌ **Memory usage** - Loads all file keys into memory before sorting
❌ **No progress bar** - Only shows individual file completion

