## How It Works

### Startup Process

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ 1. Initialize                                       │
│    • Create download directory                      │
│    • Load/create history file                       │
└─────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────┘
              ▼
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ 2. Auto-Discovery                                   │
│    • Find most recent year                          │
│    • Find most recent month                         │
│    • Find most recent day                           │
│    • Find most recent hour                          │
└─────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────┘
              ▼
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ 3. Enter Main Loop                                  │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

### Main Loop (Each Cycle)

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ 1. Query S3 for Recent Files                        │
│    aws s3api list-objects-v2                        │
│    --query "reverse(sort_by(..., &LastModified))"  │
└─────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────┘
              ▼
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ 2. Filter Files                                     │
│    • Check download history                         │
│    • Check channel match                            │
└─────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────┘
              ▼
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ 3. Download New Files (Parallel)                    │
│    • Sort by timestamp                              │
│    • Download with xargs -P                         │
│    • Mark in history                                │
└─────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────┘
              ▼
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ 4. Check for Next Hour                              │
│    • Calculate next hour timestamp                  │
│    • Check if directory exists in S3                │
│    • Auto-advance if available                      │
└─────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────┘
              ▼
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ 5. Sleep (CHECK_INTERVAL seconds)                   │
└─────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────┘
              │
              └───────────────► Loop back to step 1
```

### Hour Transition Logic

```
Current: 2025-11-07 23:00

Check next hour:
  next_epoch = current + 1 hour
  next = 2025-11-08 00:00  (auto-handles day/month/year change)

Query S3:
  aws s3 ls s3://bucket/location/2025/11/08/
  Look for: "PRE 00/"

If found:
  ✅ Move to 2025-11-08 00:00
Else:
  ⏸️  Stay at 2025-11-07 23:00
```

### Lookback Window

```
S3 Hour Directory: 19:00 - 19:59
Total files: 120

Lookback window: 20 files
  ┌───────────────────────────────────┐
  │ Most recent 20 files by           │
  │ LastModified timestamp            │
  └───────────────────────────────────┘
         ▼
  • 19:55:30 ← Newest
  • 19:55:00
  • 19:54:30
  • ...
  • 19:45:30 ← Oldest in window

Why lookback?
  • Catches late-arriving files
  • Handles out-of-order uploads
  • Balances thoroughness vs. efficiency
```

