## Download History

### Format

```bash
# .download_history.txt
nungambakkam/2025/11/14/19/channel401_20251114T190000.mp4
nungambakkam/2025/11/14/19/channel401_20251114T190030.mp4
nungambakkam/2025/11/14/19/channel701_20251114T190000.mp4
```

Each line is the full S3 key (one file per line)

### Thread Safety

```bash
# Multiple workers downloading in parallel
Worker 1: Downloading file A
  ├─ flock -x 200  (acquire lock)
  ├─ echo "key" >> history
  └─ Release lock

Worker 2: Downloading file B (waits)
  ├─ flock -x 200  (waits for lock)
  ├─ echo "key" >> history
  └─ Release lock
```

### Management

```bash
# View history
cat .download_history.txt

# Count downloaded files
wc -l .download_history.txt

# Find specific file
grep "channel401_20251114T190000" .download_history.txt

# Clear history (forces re-download)
rm .download_history.txt

# Backup history
cp .download_history.txt .download_history.backup.txt

# Remove duplicates (if any)
sort -u .download_history.txt -o .download_history.txt
```

