## Tuning Parameters

### Check Interval

```bash
CHECK_INTERVAL=90  # seconds

# Guidelines:
30-60s   → High-frequency (near real-time)
90-120s  → Balanced (recommended)
180-300s → Low-frequency (batch-like)

# Consider:
• File arrival frequency
• S3 API rate limits
• Network bandwidth
```

### Lookback Window

```bash
LOOKBACK_FILES=20

# Guidelines:
10-15  → Fast uploads, reliable timing
20-25  → Recommended for most cases
30-50  → Unreliable uploads, lots of stragglers

# Trade-offs:
Smaller → Faster checks, may miss late files
Larger  → More API calls, catches more stragglers
```

### Parallel Downloads

```bash
MAX_PARALLEL=10

# Guidelines:
5-10   → Conservative (stable)
10-20  → Aggressive (fast)
20+    → Very aggressive (may hit limits)

# Factors:
• Network bandwidth
• CPU cores
• S3 API limits
• Disk I/O
```

