## Common Features (Both Scripts)

### Timezone

Both scripts use **IST (Indian Standard Time)** internally:

```bash
ist_date() {
  TZ="Asia/Kolkata" date "$@"
}

# All timestamps are in IST
# Files are matched using IST
# Hour directories are processed in IST
```

### Channel Filtering

```bash
# Filename pattern
channel401_20251114T190530.mp4
^^^^^^^
Channel number extracted with regex: 'channel\K\d+'

# Matching logic
is_channel_match() {
  local filename="$1"
  [[ ${#CHANNELS[@]} -eq 0 ]] && return 0  # No filter = all pass
  
  local file_channel=$(echo "$filename" | grep -oP 'channel\K\d+')
  
  for chan in "${CHANNELS[@]}"; do
    [[ "$file_channel" == "$chan" ]] && return 0
  done
  
  return 1  # No match
}
```

### Error Handling

```bash
set -euo pipefail

# -e: Exit on error
# -u: Exit on undefined variable
# -o pipefail: Exit on pipe failures

# Safe command substitution
result=$(command 2>/dev/null || echo "")
[[ -z "$result" ]] && { handle_error; }
```

