## Troubleshooting

### Problem: No files downloaded

```bash
# Check 1: AWS credentials
aws s3 ls s3://anitum-jk-production/nungambakkam/ --max-items 5

# Check 2: Time range
# Ensure files exist for your specified time

# Check 3: Channel filter
# Try without --channel flag first

# Check 4: Permissions
ls -la ./P_downloaded
chmod 755 ./P_downloaded
```

### Problem: Script exits immediately

```bash
# Check logs for errors
./downloader.sh 2>&1 | tee debug.log

# Common causes:
# • Invalid time format
# • No matching files
# • AWS credential issues
# • Network connectivity
```

### Problem: Slow downloads

```bash
# Check 1: Network speed
wget -O /dev/null http://speedtest.tele2.net/10MB.zip

# Check 2: Increase parallelism
MAX_PARALLEL=20

# Check 3: EC2 placement
# Use instance in same region as S3

# Check 4: Instance type
# Ensure adequate network bandwidth
```

### Problem: Missing files (continuous mode)

```bash
# Check 1: Lookback window too small
./continuous_downloader.sh --lookback 30

# Check 2: Check interval too long
./continuous_downloader.sh --interval 60

# Check 3: Review history
grep "Skipped:" /var/log/s3-downloader.log

# Check 4: Verify S3 upload timing
aws s3api list-objects-v2 \
  --bucket anitum-jk-production \
  --prefix "nungambakkam/2025/11/14/19/" \
  --query "Contents[].[Key,LastModified]" \
  --output table
```

### Problem: Duplicate downloads

```bash
# One-time downloader: Expected (no duplicate check)
# Continuous downloader: Should not happen

# If it happens:
# Check 1: History file corrupted
sort -u .download_history.txt -o .download_history.txt

# Check 2: Multiple instances running
ps aux | grep continuous_downloader
# Kill duplicates

# Check 3: History file permissions
ls -la .download_history.txt
chmod 644 .download_history.txt
```

### Problem: Out of disk space

```bash
# Check space
df -h ./P_downloaded

# Solution 1: Move files after download
# (history tracking handles this)

# Solution 2: Add auto-cleanup
find ./P_downloaded -type f -mtime +7 -delete

# Solution 3: External processing
rsync -av --remove-source-files ./P_downloaded/ /mnt/storage/
```

